{
  "strategy": "Ground the original unsolved geometry diagram first, then use chart/diagram interpretation on that frame bundle to read the labeled angles and structural relations needed to compute angle BDC. Keep the plan minimal and avoid broad video understanding since the question is about a single static diagram near the start.",
  "tool_calls": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "tool": "frame_retriever",
      "arguments": {
        "video_path": "VIDEO",
        "query": "original geometry problem diagram with triangle labeled A B C and angle BDC marked in green, before any worked-solution annotations are added",
        "timestamps": null,
        "num_frames": 3
      },
      "purpose": "Retrieve candidate frames of the question-bearing geometry diagram in its unsolved state so later analysis reads the correct visual phase rather than an explanation frame.",
      "depends_on": []
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tool": "chart_analyzer",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null,
        "query": "geometry diagram: identify all visible labeled points, angle markings, given angle values, equal-length marks, and which rays/segments form angle BDC marked in green"
      },
      "purpose": "Interpret the structured geometry figure and extract the exact labels, marked angles, and segment relationships needed for reasoning about angle BDC.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tool": "ocr",
      "arguments": {
        "frame_path": "<STEP_1:frames>",
        "timestamp": null
      },
      "purpose": "Verify the visible text labels and numeric angle values on the same candidate frames in case the diagram interpreter misses or paraphrases small labels.",
      "depends_on": [
        1
      ]
    }
  ],
  "refinement_instructions": "Write a first trace from scratch. Use step 1 only to identify the correct unsolved diagram frame among the returned candidates; do not assume retrieval rank implies correctness. Then use the frame-level result from step 2 for the candidate frame that actually shows the original problem. Cite the diagram evidence explicitly: labeled points, equal-length marks, given angle values, and the rays that define green angle BDC. Use step 3 to confirm exact text/numbers/labels if any are small or ambiguous in step 2. In the rewritten trace, first describe the grounded diagram structure, then perform only the geometry derivation supported by those grounded givens, and finally map the computed angle to the matching option. If the verified value contradicts any tentative intuition, update the answer to the option matching the computed measure. If any label or value remains unreadable, state that uncertainty rather than guessing."
}
